n servicemen and the things they carried.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/places/000/vietnam-veterans-memorial-three-servicemen-statue.htm","source_title":"Vietnam Veterans Memorial: Three Servicemen Statue","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2022-12-13","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor memorial area; follow posted site guidance.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"vietnam-womens-memorial","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Vietnam Women’s Memorial","title":"Pause at the Vietnam Women’s Memorial","subtitle":"Constitution Avenue NW corridor","notes":"Visit the bronze group south of the Vietnam Veterans Memorial and take time to notice the three women caring for a wounded soldier.","short_summary":"A figurative memorial recognizing women who served during the Vietnam War.","evidence_claim":"NPS identifies the Vietnam Women’s Memorial as a sculpture of three uniformed women caring for a wounded male soldier.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/places/000/vietnam-womens-memorial.htm","source_title":"Vietnam Women’s Memorial","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor National Mall memorial; follow posted site guidance.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"vietnam-in-memory-plaque","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Vietnam Veterans Memorial: In Memory Plaque","title":"Find the In Memory plaque","subtitle":"Constitution Avenue NW corridor","notes":"Look in the northeast corner of the Three Servicemen plaza for this later addition honoring Vietnam veterans who died from service-related causes.","short_summary":"A 2004 plaque expands the memorial’s act of remembrance.","evidence_claim":"NPS says the In Memory plaque, dedicated in 2004, honors Vietnam veterans who later died from causes related to the war.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/places/000/vietnam-veterans-memorial-in-memory-plaque.htm","source_title":"Vietnam Veterans Memorial: In Memory Plaque","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2022-12-13","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor memorial area; follow posted site guidance.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"constitution-gardens","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Constitution Gardens","title":"Cross to Signers Island","subtitle":"Constitution Avenue NW corridor","notes":"Use the footbridge on the north side of the pond to reach the memorial to the 56 signers of the Declaration of Independence.","short_summary":"A landscaped park with a pond, paths, and an island memorial.","evidence_claim":"NPS notes that Constitution Gardens has a pond and that Signers Island, with its 56-signers memorial, is reached by footbridge.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/coga/planyourvisit/basicinfo.htm","source_title":"Constitution Gardens: Basic Information","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2016-03-04","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"NPS lists the site as open 24 hours; facilities may close in the evening.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lincoln-memorial","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Lincoln Memorial","title":"Step into the Lincoln Memorial chamber","subtitle":"23rd Street NW corridor","notes":"Approach from the Reflecting Pool and view the seated Lincoln statue and interior inscriptions in the memorial’s main chamber.","short_summary":"The chamber is the principal public space within the Lincoln Memorial.","evidence_claim":"NPS states that the Lincoln Memorial is free and open to the public, including the chamber with the Lincoln statue and symbolic features.","source_url":"https://home.nps.gov/linc/planyourvisit/fees.htm","source_title":"Lincoln Memorial: Fees & Passes","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2026-05-26","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The main memorial is free; the lower-level museum and undercroft require timed entry.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"korean-war-veterans-memorial","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Korean War Veterans Memorial","title":"Follow the 19-statue patrol","subtitle":"23rd Street NW corridor","notes":"Walk the memorial’s Field of Service and look for the nineteen stainless-steel figures whose reflections create an image of thirty-eight.","short_summary":"A memorial with a field of stainless-steel soldier figures and reflective surfaces.","evidence_claim":"NPS describes nineteen stainless-steel statues whose reflections create the visual effect of 38 figures.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/places/000/korean-war-veterans-memorial.htm","source_title":"Korean War Veterans Memorial","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2025-12-30","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"NPS lists the memorial as open 24 hours a day, every day of the year.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"district-of-columbia-war-memorial","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"District of Columbia War Memorial","title":"Look up inside the DC War Memorial","subtitle":"Independence Avenue SW corridor","notes":"Step beneath the open circular pavilion south of the Reflecting Pool and look for the names carved around its marble base.","short_summary":"A local World War I memorial designed as an open Doric pavilion.","evidence_claim":"NPS identifies this as a World War I memorial with an open circular Doric structure and the names of 499 honored Washingtonians.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/places/000/district-of-columbia-war-memorial.htm","source_title":"District of Columbia War Memorial","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2025-12-03","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor National Mall memorial; follow posted site guidance.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"world-war-ii-memorial","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"World War II Memorial","title":"Walk the World War II Memorial plaza","subtitle":"17th Street NW corridor","notes":"Enter the memorial between the Lincoln Memorial and Washington Monument and trace the state and territorial pillars around the central fountain.","short_summary":"A National Mall memorial positioned between the Lincoln Memorial and Washington Monument.","evidence_claim":"NPS includes the World War II Memorial among the sites preserved by National Mall and Memorial Parks.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/visit-national-mall-and-memorial-parks.htm","source_title":"Visit National Mall and Memorial Parks","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor National Mall memorial; follow posted site guidance.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"albert-einstein-memorial","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Albert Einstein Memorial","title":"Visit the Albert Einstein Memorial","subtitle":"Constitution Avenue NW corridor","notes":"Stop at the National Academy of Sciences grounds to see the Einstein memorial, unveiled for the centennial of the scientist’s birth.","short_summary":"A memorial sculpture on the National Academy of Sciences grounds.","evidence_claim":"The National Academy of Sciences states that the Albert Einstein Memorial was unveiled in 1979 and stands on the Academy grounds.","source_url":"https://www.nasonline.org/about-the-nas/locations/","source_title":"National Academy of Sciences Locations","source_kind":"other_reliable","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The memorial is on Academy grounds; the NAS Building itself is closed to the public except for authorized visitors.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
